# PR Review Correction Loop (Pre-Merge)

Merge to `main` only when the **dual gate** holds on the same latest head SHA:
**blocking CI is green** and **automated review feedback has reached quiescence**,
including the **arrival wait**. Neither half is enough. Human modus operandi:
`docs/pr-merge-gate.md`.

Complements `@.cursor/rules/011-coderabbit-pr-gate.mdc` (authoritative predicate)
and `@.cursor/rules/012-dependabot-pr-gate.mdc` (Dependabot).

## Bots in scope (address every actionable item)

| Source | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| **CodeRabbit** (`coderabbitai`) | Inline threads + **review body** (out-of-diff findings often appear only in the summary). A check that only says **“Review rate limited”** is **not** quiescence — parse **Next review available in: N minutes**, wait `N+buffer`, then post `@coderabbitai review` and repeat until a real review targets the latest head. **After 3 failed wait/re-trigger cycles, or a single wait exceeding 90 minutes, with no real CodeRabbit review yet posted for the current head** — this exact threshold, repeated verbatim in `011` and `docs/pr-merge-gate.md` — CodeRabbit becomes optional as a blocker via `011` step 6 **(b)** Sourcery stand-in or **(c)** 2026-09-03 skip — see `011` step 7. A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review is never optional-away. |
| **CodeAnt** (`codeant-ai`) | Inline suggestions + quality-gate status. **“🔄 Reviewing your PR…”** is in-progress — not quiescence. |
| **Sourcery** (`sourcery-ai`) | Comment `@sourcery-ai review` only when the latest review predates the current head **and** the 250k / 7-day budget is **not** exhausted. Auto “Reviewer’s Guide” is not a real review. Inline `suggestion` / `nitpick` / `suggestion (bug_risk)`; `bug_risk` findings are correctness bugs. |
| **Copilot** (`copilot-pull-request-reviewer`) | Inline PR review comments. Wait if the review check is still pending. |
| **DeepSource** (`deepsource-io`) | **Mandatory:** post `@deepsourcebot review` on every PR (open + after fix pushes). Team AI Review is on-demand; without that mention only static analysis runs. Address AI Review + actionable Docker/Shell findings. Dashboard JS analyzer remains off — see `docs/deepsource-javascript-ci.md`. |
| **CodeScene** | Address actionable comments when the check runs. Docs-only PRs may skip with no app code. |
| **Socket Security** | Actionable PR alerts when they block merge |
| **Cursor Bugbot** | When explicitly requested |
| **Greptile / Codex** | Skip when trial or usage limits return no review (document in PR disposition comment) |

Human review comments requesting concrete fixes are in scope while open.

## Merge gate order (strict)

1. **Push** fix commits to the PR branch. Do **not** use `git commit --no-verify` / `git push --no-verify`.
2. **Trigger** `@deepsourcebot review` (required on open and after **every** fix push), `@coderabbitai review` whenever the latest head lacks a real CodeRabbit review (missing, stale SHA, or rate-limited placeholder), and `@sourcery-ai review` only when the latest head lacks a Sourcery review **and** the 250k / 7-day budget is not exhausted.
3. **Wait** for blocking CI on the latest commit (`deploy.yml` Typecheck/Lint/Tests, build, security audit, Chromium + cross-browser E2E — read job logs, not badge alone for advisory jobs).
4. **Arrival wait:** do not collect-and-merge while an in-scope bot is still in-progress on the current head (CodeAnt “🔄 Reviewing…”, pending Greptile / Copilot / CodeScene / CodeRabbit). GraphQL `reviewThreads` = 0 is not quiescence if a bot has not finished arriving (PR #299).
5. **Collect** all open review threads (GraphQL `reviewThreads`) and scan **every** bot and human review body posted for the current head — not just the single latest one — for new actionable items (include DeepSource AI Review + CodeRabbit summary, and any top-level human review body). A later empty or approval-only review does not retract an earlier body-only finding on the same head. **CodeRabbit "outside diff range" findings never appear as GraphQL `reviewThreads`**. Fetch full review bodies via `gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/N/reviews --paginate` and grep for `outside diff` (case-insensitive) on **every** pass. **Track each body-only finding in a disposition ledger** (`fixed` / `replied` / `deferred`) before declaring quiescence.
6. **Fix or reply** on every thread and every tracked body-only finding; **resolve** threads after fix or documented rationale.
7. **Re-check** after bots finish on the new commit. For CodeRabbit rate limits: parse the wait time, sleep through it (+buffer), re-trigger `@coderabbitai review` (bounded loop in `011` — 3 failed cycles or a single wait exceeding 90 minutes, **only** while no real review yet exists for the current head). After that threshold, CodeRabbit is optional as a blocker via `011` step 6 **(b)** or **(c)**. **Do not merge** while CodeRabbit `CHANGES_REQUESTED` targets the **latest** head — never waived by the optional-CodeRabbit condition. The same applies to an **active human `CHANGES_REQUESTED`**. Also do not merge while DeepSource AI Review was never attempted on the latest head, or while unresolved threads or untracked body-only findings remain. A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review on a **superseded** commit is not a merge block once a newer real review exists for the current head.
8. **Merge** only when step 3 is green **and** step 7 shows quiescence (arrival wait complete, no new actionable items). Green CI alone is not enough.

Do **not** merge on stale bot approval from an older commit while newer commits are untested or unreviewed.

## Correction loop (per finding)

1. Verify against **current** code on the PR branch (bots often comment on superseded commits).
2. **Fix** if valid; prefer minimal, focused diffs.
3. **Defer** only with a short English reply on the thread (rare — security/correctness findings should be fixed).
4. **Reply** on the inline thread citing the fixing commit — **only when a thread exists**. A body-only finding (no thread ID) has no thread to reply on; record its disposition in the ledger and/or a PR disposition comment instead.
5. **Resolve** the review thread (GitHub “Resolve conversation”).
6. Post a **PR disposition comment** when closing a large batch (bot → action table).

## CI vs advisory checks

- **Blocking:** `deploy.yml` quality gates, Chromium E2E (`e2e.yml`), cross-browser E2E (`e2e-cross-browser.yml` — Firefox/WebKit/mobile Chrome), required branch protections, Socket when flagged blocking.
- **Advisory (default):** DeepSource JavaScript (`deepsourceJavaScriptAdvisory: true`), Claude Code skipped jobs on PRs without `@claude`.
- **Claude Code `action_required`:** Workflow triggered by `pull_request_review_comment` may show **Approve and run workflows** with zero jobs — GitHub workflow-approval gate, not a failed test. Job `if` still requires `@claude` in the comment body.

## Collection commands (agents / maintainers)

```bash
# Unresolved threads with author
gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:"qnbs", name:"AI-Research-Orchestrator") { pullRequest(number:N) { reviewThreads(first:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(last:1) { nodes { databaseId author { login } body } } } } } } }'

# Every review body (grep outside-diff / CHANGES_REQUESTED / Reviewing)
gh api repos/qnbs/AI-Research-Orchestrator/pulls/N/reviews --paginate

# Latest CodeRabbit review commit
gh api repos/qnbs/AI-Research-Orchestrator/pulls/N/reviews --jq '[.[]|select(.user.login=="coderabbitai[bot]")]|sort_by(.submitted_at)|.[-1]'
```

Replace `N` with the PR number. After fixes, resolve threads via GraphQL `resolveReviewThread` or the GitHub UI.

## Lessons (standing)

- **Align identifiers end-to-end:** UI label, external URL, export/PDF, and corpus keys must use the same resolved identifier (P1-5 lesson).
- **Canonical legacy keys win:** When `pmid` and `articleId` disagree, trust the canonical `pmid` string for maps and hydration.
- **Hydrate before validation:** Run `ensureGroundedClaim` / `ensureArticleIdentifiers` before corpus validation and Dexie upgrades; guard non-string legacy keys.
- **i18n for all identifier types:** Copy toast and ARIA labels must not hard-code “PMID” when DOI/arXiv/PMCID are copied.
- **DOI URLs:** Use `encodeURI` for `doi.org` paths (preserve `/`); do not `encodeURIComponent` the full DOI.
- **CodeRabbit re-reviews** each push — expect 2–4 correction rounds on medium PRs. Rate-limit placeholders must be waited out and re-triggered (`@coderabbitai review`); never treat “Review rate limited” as approval.
- **Outside-diff-range findings hide from thread sweeps.** A GraphQL `reviewThreads` query that returns 0 unresolved can still hide a finding in a review's raw `body` (CodeRabbit "⚠️ Outside diff range comments"). Confirmed on PR #220. Always run both checks.
- **Arrival wait (PR #299):** Required CI + quality gates were green and threads were empty; the PR was merged while CodeAnt was still “🔄 Reviewing…” and Greptile had not arrived. A P2 (missing **Impact** on a meeting-note entry) landed after merge. Thread count 0 is not quiescence if a bot is still arriving.
- **Heavy same-PR bot activity can rate-limit reviews on other PRs.** CodeRabbit fair-usage appears repo/org-wide. If two PRs land together, budget the wait.
- **Sourcery budget (2026-09):** Do not `@sourcery-ai review` while 250k diff-characters / 7 days is exhausted. Sourcery cannot stand in for CodeRabbit in that window — use `011` step 6 **(c)**.
- **DeepSource noise:** JavaScript analyzer is off in the DeepSource dashboard; `.deepsource.toml` has no `javascript` block (`docs/deepsource-dashboard-off.md`).

